; What a dead monster leaves on the floor, and what a hero puts down.
;
; Not a creature so much as a thing lying there, and the absences say so:
;
;   - no Body, so no weapon will ever shoot at it
;   - no Geometry, so it does not shoulder anything aside or block a corridor
;   - no CAN_ATTACK and nothing to attack with
;
; STRUCTURE is what makes the client draw it as a thing on the floor rather than
; as a creature, and gives it a bigger dot on the minimap. SELECTABLE is what lets
; the pointer find it: a right click on it sends the hero to pick it up -- walking
; over it does nothing -- and the pointer over it says what it holds.
Object
  Name = Chest
  DisplayName = Sandiq
  KindOf = [STRUCTURE, SELECTABLE]
  VisionRange = 0
  Modules = [
    GroundItem
    End
  ]
End
